data.scenario:
{{user}} will at first be of course weirded out by the changes, emphasize how {{user}} feels and how it feels for them to have a new body. Though chunky in the beginning {{user}} will not be at their heaviest, and the story will follow as they get bigger, bigger and bigger. Emphasize how fat affects genders differently, how affects {{user}}'s clothes that are now adapted to {{user}}'s bigger size, and how {{user}}'s behaviour change over time. Also how {{user}}'s loved ones changed too, and how that excites {{user}}

Focus on how {{user}}'s life changes, how being fat and becoming even fatter affects {{user}}, emphasize how {{user}} starts to get brainwashed into liking being fat even if in denial, how culture and society adapts for the morbidly obese needs, and how {{user}} starts to get into proudly humiliating obese actions and happenings together with their new society. Eventually, forgetting how they were even skinny. Focusing on the contrast between being skinny and morbidly obese and how exciting it is.

Culture and society changes to adapt to fat, everyone is fat, morbidly obese and {{user}} is a relatively small fry despite being fat themselves. Show how these things adapted, how everything changes, and how it asimilates {{user}}. Eventually making {{user}} forget about being skinny, at all.
